{"id": "q0293", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 29.45, "n_chunks": 30, "scores": [0.4261, 0.391, 0.2932, 0.3071, 0.336, 0.3929, 0.3474, 0.3564, 0.2912, 0.389, 0.5726, 0.3996, 0.2626, 0.2501, 0.243, 0.1693, 0.3214, 0.3965, 0.3463, 0.2881, 0.3917, 0.3351, 0.3224, 0.3691, 0.3428, 0.435, 0.4364, 0.316, 0.3476, 0.4083], "eot_score": 0.4956, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": "I. shape constancy", "query": "Young Tina had never seen the space shuttle until her parents pointed out a picture of it ready to launch. When she next saw a picture of it flying, she had difficulty recognizing it. Which concept best explains this problem?\n\nA. dishabituation\nB. sensory adaptation\nC. perceptual adaptation\nD. summation\nE. perceptual set\nF. sensory interaction\nG. binocular cue\nH. depth perception\nI. shape constancy\nJ. autokinetic effect\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "transcript": "Young Tina had never seen the space shuttle until her parents pointed out a picture of it ready to launch. When she next saw a picture of it flying, she had difficulty recognizing it. Which concept best explains this problem? A) dishabituation, B) sensory adaptation, C) perceptual adaptation, D) summation, E) perceptual set, F) sensory interaction, G) binocular cue, H) depth perception, I) shape constancy, J) autokinetic effect.", "mode": "local", "answer": "E. Perceptual set.", "answer_ms": 234}
{"id": "q0308", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 3.64, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [0.5123, 0.4089, 0.3679, 0.381], "eot_score": 0.7213, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "Mary holding the dead body of", "query": "In Christian art what does a painting termed a ‘Pieta’ depict?", "transcript": "In Christian art, what does a painting termed a pietà depict?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "A *pietà*, or *pity*, depicts the Virgin Mary mourning over the dead body of Jesus Christ, usually holding him after the Crucifixion.", "expert_answer": "A **pietà** depicts the **Virgin Mary mourning over the dead body of Jesus Christ**, usually holding him after the Crucifixion.", "expert_latency_s": 3.83, "stall_ms": 31, "relay_ms": 1030}
