{"id": "q0409", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 3.01, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [0.4748, 0.4155, 0.3716, 0.4154], "eot_score": 0.9302, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What is the Philly Special and when was it used ?", "transcript": "What is the Philly Special and when was it used?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The Philly Special was a famous trick play run by the Philadelphia Eagles in Super Bowl LII against the New England Patriots. It was used on February 4, 2018, near the end of the first half, on 4th-and-goal. Eagles quarterback Nick Foles lined up as if he were changing the play, the ball was snapped directly to running back Corey Clement, handed to tight end Trey Burton, and Burton threw a touchdown pass to Foles. The play helped the Eagles win 41–33, giving them their first Super Bowl title.", "expert_answer": "The **Philly Special** was a famous trick play run by the **Philadelphia Eagles** in **Super Bowl LII** against the **New England Patriots**.\n\nIt was used on **February 4, 2018**, near the end of the **first half**, on **4th-and-goal**. Eagles quarterback **Nick Foles** lined up as if he were changing the play, the ball was snapped directly to running back **Corey Clement**, handed to tight end **Trey Burton**, and Burton threw a touchdown pass to Foles.\n\nThe play helped the Eagles win **41–33**, giving them their first Super Bowl title.", "expert_latency_s": 5.34, "stall_ms": 32, "relay_ms": 4062}
