{"id": "q0426", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.9, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.4051, 0.3532, 0.3358], "eot_score": 0.2399, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What is the purpose of a shot clock in basketball?", "transcript": "What is the purpose of a shot clock in basketball?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The purpose of a shot clock in basketball is to keep the pace of the game moving by requiring teams to attempt a shot on goal within a certain amount of time after gaining possession of the ball. The shot clock ensures that play does not stall for extended periods, promoting more dynamic and continuous action. In professional leagues like the NBA, the standard shot clock allows 24 seconds; other levels may use different times. If a team fails to take a shot within the allotted time, they typically lose possession of the ball. This rule helps maintain excitement and flow in the game.", "answer_ms": 3667}
